      "text": "The patient presents with complaints of fatigue, flank pain, and a persistent fever. She reports that these symptoms have continued despite the resolution of her sinusitis symptoms. She was initially treated with amoxicillin for acute sinusitis for 12 days, during which she developed a rash. The antibiotic was then changed to cephalexin for an additional week, and the rash resolved. She has a medical history of essential hypertension, hyperlipidemia, and gastric reflux and has been on a stable regimen of lisinopril, simvastatin, and omeprazole."
